			"Message": "docs(Output): Expand architectural comments across pipeline, ESBuild, plugins, and polyfills\n\nThe Output component (bundled JS artifacts for Cocoon runtime) previously had minimal\ninline documentation. This commit adds comprehensive architectural context to every\nmajor configuration module explaining WHY each transform, polyfill, copy operation,\nand exclusion exists — not just WHAT it does.\n\nKey additions:\n- Pipeline.js: Each ServiceCopy entry now documents the source authored location,\n  the reverse-hierarchical split naming convention, and why destination filenames\n  retain legacy compound names to match runtime import strings.\n- ESBuild exclusion modules (Electron, Node, Network, Telemetry, Test, etc.):\n  Comments now distinguish between abstract interfaces (kept) vs Electron/Node\n  implementations (excluded), and explain the Mountain/Cocoon gRPC replacement\n  strategy for each stripped subsystem.\n- Plugin transforms: Every Match/Transform now includes the architectural\n  rationale — e.g., ReplaceElectronIPCService explains the TauriMainProcessService\n  shim, InjectPartZIndexCSS documents the menubar clipping bug it prevents.\n- Polyfills (ChildProcess, FileSystem, IPC, NativeModule, Process, SharedProcess):\n  Comments trace each stubbed Electron API to its Mountain IPC route or explain\n  why a no-op is safe (e.g., telemetryAppender no-op because Land centralizes\n  telemetry via Mountain's PostHog bridge).\n- TauriMainProcessService: ChannelRouteMap now documents every routed channel\n  with the VS Code callsite that depends on it (e.g., extensionManagement\n  routed because Extensions sidebar calls getInstalled via that channel).\n- SharedProcessProxy: Each service proxy's health check and stub shape explained.\n\nNo behavioral changes — only documentation/comment expansion to make the\nElectron→Tauri+Effect-TS architecture self-documenting for future maintainers.",
			"SHA": "5c892147b3255d966a599dc5bd527cc8da761598"
		},
